          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वसतिः (vasatiḥ) is built on the root √vas, \"to dwell, to stay\", which also gives vasati, \"dwells\"; MW gives the noun vasati as staying, especially overnight, a dwelling (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
